thing inside, and put all your attention\f44  on it.  \expnd-1\expndtw-5 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 he attention should be one-pointed, but gentle,\f44  and not hard concentration.\expnd0\expndtw0 \par\pard\li2264\fi-2160\ri441\sl-310\slmult0\sb72\f52\fs26\b1 Dhyana\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \f50\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex133 \uc1\u9135?\f37\charscalex100            \expnd3\expndtw14  \f44\expnd0\expndtw-2 As you totally focus on the object of your attention,\f44  notice that the awareness begins to expand outward.\f44  Let it go outward as far as it will go.\expnd0\expndtw0 \par\pard\li2264\fi-2160\ri346\sl-310\slmult0\sb72\f52\fs26\b1 Samadhi\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \f50\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex133 \uc1\u9135?\f37\charscalex100          \expnd-1\expndtw-7  \f44\expnd0\expndtw-2 When it expands to infinity then you are in the void.\f44  \expnd-1\expndtw-5 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 here is a moment of suspension, or no thoughts and\f44  no object of consciousness:  as if there were\f44  consciousness itself with nothing that you were\f44  \expnd0\expndtw0 conscious\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 of.\par\pard\li104\ri533\sl-310\slmult0\sb61\f44\fs26\expnd-1\expndtw-5 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 he last three are called Sanyama, and involve taking something into\f44  the void.\expnd0\expndtw0 \par\pard\sl-120\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\li104\ri525\qj\sl-310\slmult0\f44\fs26\expnd0\expndtw-2 At the deepest level of the mind just before Samadhi, there is a place\f44  \expnd0\expndtw0 called\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 “Rityam\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Bhara\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Pragyam,”\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 “th\expnd0\expndtw-2 at place which knows only truth,”\f44  which is similar to the Hawaiian “I’o”.\expnd0\expndtw0 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-282\slmult0\fs28 \par\pard\li4434\sl-200\slmult0\f44\fs20\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 h\expnd0\expndtw0 e\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 NLP\expnd0\ex