\li1543\sl-610\slmult0\f20\fs56\b1 V \fs34\up20\charscalex99 C\charscalex100     \expnd4\expndtw18  \fs56\expnd30\expndtw149\up0  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd-1\expndtw-3 V\fs34\expnd0\expndtw-2\up20\charscalex99  R\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\up0\charscalex100 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-109\slmult0\fs10 \par\pard\li1543\sl-610\slmult0\f20\fs56\b1\expnd0\expndtw-2 A\fs34\up20\charscalex99  \expnd0\expndtw0 C\charscalex100      \expnd-5\expndtw-23  \fs56\expnd30\expndtw149\up0  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd-1\expndtw-3 A\fs34\expnd0\expndtw-2\up20\charscalex99  R\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\up0\charscalex100 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-220\slmult0\fs22 \par\pard\li1543\sl-620\slmult0\f20\fs56\b1 K\expnd16\expndtw82  \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd30\expndtw149  \expnd0\expndtw0   A\expnd-16\expndtw-78  \fs34\expnd0\expndtw0\dn10\charscalex99 D\b0\up0\charscalex100 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-245\slmult0\fs24 \par\pard\li1262\sl-280\slmult0\f75\fs28\i1\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex99 EYE\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 MOVEMEN\expnd0\expndtw0 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 S\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 —\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 NORMAL\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 R\expnd-2\expndtw-11 I\expnd0\expndtw-2 GH\expnd0\expndtw0 T \expnd0\expndtw-2 HANDED\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 PERSON\i0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 \par\pard\sl-161\slmult0\fs16 \par\pard\li4553\ri4569\qc\sl-240\slmult0\f20\fs24\b1 Figure 1\b0 \par\pard\li2484\sl-220\slmult0\sb42\f30\fs22\charscalex98 (\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 his is h\expnd0\expndtw-2 o\expnd0\expndtw0 w they l\expnd0\expndtw-2 ook\expnd0\expndtw0  when y\expnd0\expndtw-2 ou'\expnd0\expndtw0 re facing them.)\charscalex100 \par\pard\sl-263\slmult0\fs26 \par\pard\li104\ri397\sl-330\slmult0\f30\fs28\charscalex99 When eliciting strategies from eye patt\expnd0\expndtw-2 e\expnd0\expndtw0 rns it’s important to make sure\f30  that you are learning the eye patterns for\charscalex100  \f6\charscalex99 “\f30 other\expnd0\expndtw-2 s\f6\expnd0\expndtw-2 ”\f30\expnd0\expndtw0 , not for\charscalex100  \f6\charscalex99 “\f30\expnd0\expndtw-2 sel\expnd0\expndtw0 f\f6\expnd0\expndtw-2 ”\f30\expnd0\expndtw0 .  I’ve\f30  seen people struggle for years trying to figure out what they are doing\f30  themselves.  So this is for others.\charscalex100 \par\pard\sl-122\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\li104\ri264\sl-330\slmult0\f30\fs28\expnd-1\expndtw-3\charscalex99 T\expnd0\expndtw0 he first thing to remember is that not every eye movement you see is a\f30  strategy.  Some people are going to process the information you just\f30  asked them before they begin accessing their strategy.  \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 hey may, for\f30  example, repeat to themselves exactly what you said,\expnd-1\expndtw-3\charscalex100  \f6\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex99 “\f30 Oh, he just said\charscalex100 \par\pard\li104\ri122\sl-330\slmult0\sb2\f30\fs28\charscalex99 'beautiful watch', how did I get it?  A\expnd-1\expndtw-3 n\expnd0\expndtw0 d then they'll run their strategy for\f30  you with their eyes.  Some people will immediately understand what you\f30  said and jump directly into the strategy, moving their eyes in a certain\f30  direction as they access their strategies.  Most people will move their\f30  eyes in a recognizable pattern as they access their strategy or as they\f30  replay the information in their head.  \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 he question is, do they move\charscalex100 \par\pard\li104\ri282\sl-330\slmult0\sb2\f30\fs28\charscalex99 their eyes so that you can see them adequately?  And that's where your\f30  sensory acuity becomes very, very important.  \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 hat's where your\f30  sensory acuity makes a major difference.  My suggestion is that you\f30  make sure that you've gotten really wel\expnd-1\expndtw-4 l\f6\expnd0\expndtw0 –\f30 grounded in the eye patterns,\charscalex100 \par\pard\li103\sl-280\slmult0\sb52\f30\fs28\charscalex99 and that you learn them very well.  Having done that, you can just relax\charscalex100 \par\pard\sl-267\slmult0\fs26 \par\pard\li5154\sl-200\slmult0\f30\fs20\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 h\expnd0\expndtw0 e\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 NLP\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Mas\expnd0\expndtw-2 t\expnd0\expndtw0 e\expnd0\expndtw-2 r \expnd0\expndtw0 P\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 ac\expnd0\expndtw-2 titi\expnd0\expndtw0 o\expnd-1\expndtw-3 n\expnd0\expndtw0 e\expnd0\expndtw-2 r \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 aining\expnd0\expndtw-2 ,  \expnd0\expndtw0 July\expnd0\expndtw-2 , \expnd0\expndtw0 2004\par\pard\li3695\sl-240\slmult0\sb8\f30\fs20\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Copy\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 ight \f47\charscalex107 ©\f30\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100  \expnd0\expndtw0 1987-2004\expnd0\expndtw-2 , \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 ad\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 James\expnd0\expndtw-2 , \expnd0\expndtw0 Advanced\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Neu\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 o\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Dynamics\par\pard\sect\sectd\sbkpage\marglsxn1480\margrsxn600\margtsxn760\li8779\sl-360\slmult0\sb14\f26\fs36 Six\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 …\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 5\par\pard\li104\ri257\sl-330\slmult0\sb3\f30\fs28\charscalex99 and let the information come to you.  Just watch their eye patterns and\f30  then note them on a piece of paper\expnd-1\expndtw-4\charscalex100  \f6\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex99 —\f30  one of the things I do is carry a\f30  little piece of paper with me, and write down the order and sequence of\f30  their eye patterns as I get them, so I'll remember them\expnd-1\expndtw-3\charscalex100  \f6\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex99 —\f30  \expnd0\expndtw-2 and\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 note\f30  \expnd0\expndtw0 them, using the notation form above.\charscalex100 \par\pard\li104\ri134\sl-330\slmult0\sb2\f30\fs28\charscalex99 I suggest that as with any strategy elicitation, you also test the strategy\f30  elicitation from eye patterns wherever possible, questioning them over\f30  and over again, until you're sure you've got it.  It's OK to check several\f30  times because the major question in t\expnd-1\expndtw-3 h\expnd0\expndtw0 e elicitation of strategies from eye\f30  patterns is,\charscalex100  \f6\charscalex99 “\f30 Where does the accessing of the information end and the\f30  strategy begin?\f6\expnd0\expndtw-2 ”\f30\expnd0\expndtw0   So you may have to elicit the same strategy in a couple\f30  of different situations, or a couple of different contexts in order to\f30  discover how did they do it.\charscalex100 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-134\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\li104\ri381\sl-330\slmult0\f30\fs28\charscalex99 Strategies from eye patterns are probably one of the most powerful\f30  things that you can learn in NLP, and in a later chapter we'll put it all\f30  together when we show how to utilize those strategies in designing\f30  \expnd0\expndtw-2 embedded\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 commands.\expnd0\expndtw0   \expnd0\expndtw-2 Let's\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 elicit\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 s\expnd-1\expndtw-3 o\expnd0\expndtw0 me strategies, now ... below, we’ve\f30  included transcripts of actual strategy elicitations:\charscalex100 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-220\slmult0\fs22 \par\pard\li5154\sl-200\slmult0\f30\fs20\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 h\expnd0\expndtw0 e\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 NLP\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Mas\expnd0\expndtw-2 t\expnd0\expndtw0 e\expnd0\expndtw-2 r \expnd0\expndtw0 P\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 ac\expnd0\expndtw-2 titi\expnd0\expndtw0 o\expnd-1\expndtw-3 n\expnd0\expndtw0 e\expnd0\expndtw-2 r \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 aining\expnd0\expndtw-2 ,  \expnd0\expndtw0 July\expnd0\expndtw-2 , \expnd0\expndtw0 2004\par\pard\li3695\sl-240\slmult0\sb8\f30\fs20\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Copy\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 ight \f47\charscalex107 ©\f30\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100  \expnd0\expndtw0 1987-2004\expnd0\expndtw-2 , \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 ad\exp