ey describe.\par\pard\sl-166\slmult0\fs16 \par\pard\li104\sl-240\slmult0\f30\fs24  3.    \expnd7\expndtw35  \expnd0\expndtw0 Auditory digital is valuable as a filing system:\par\pard\li824\sl-290\slmult0\sb6\f47\fs24\charscalex131 •\f37\charscalex100          \expnd2\expndtw9  \f30\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 o keep track of experience.\par\pard\li824\sl-290\slmult0\sb6\f47\fs24\charscalex131 •\f37\charscalex100          \expnd2\expndtw9  \f30\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 o categorize experience.\par\pard\li824\sl-290\slmult0\sb6\f47\fs24\charscalex131 •\f37\charscalex100          \expnd2\expndtw9  \f30\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 o set direction.\par\pard\li824\sl-290\slmult0\sb6\f47\fs24\charscalex131 •\f37\charscalex100          \expnd2\expndtw9  \f30\expnd0\expndtw-2 To\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 plan.\expnd0\expndtw0 \par\pard\li824\sl-290\slmult0\sb6\f47\fs24\charscalex131 •\f37\charscalex100          \expnd2\expndtw9  \f30\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 o summarize.\par\pard\li824\sl-290\slmult0\sb6\f47\fs24\charscalex131 •\f37\charscalex100          \expnd2\expndtw9  \f30\expnd0\expndtw-2 To\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 make\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 a\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 running\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 commentary\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 on\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 raw\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 data.\expnd0\expndtw0 \par\pard\li824\sl-290\slmult0\sb6\f47\fs24\charscalex131 •\f37\charscalex100          \expnd2\expndtw9  \f30\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 o draw conclusions.\par\pard\li824\sl-290\slmult0\sb6\f47\fs24\charscalex131 •\f37\charscalex100          \expnd2\expndtw9  \f30\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 o make sense of things.\par\pard\sl-166\slmult0\fs16 \par\pard\li104\sl-240\slmult0\f30\fs24  4.    \expnd7\expndtw34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Auditory tonal can add emphasis and help flesh out raw data.\par\pard\sl-126\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\li104\ri1021\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24  5.    \expnd7\expndtw34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Visual can represent an enormous amount of data simultaneously and\f30  instantaneously.\par\pard\sl-126\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\li104\ri690\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24  6.    \expnd7\expndtw34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Auditory processing is sequential and takes longer than visual processing\f30  which is simultaneous.\par\pard\sl-126\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\li104\ri648\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24  7.    \expnd7\expndtw34  \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 he kinesthetic system has more inertia and duration than the visual and\f30  auditory systems.\par\pard\sl-126\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\li104\ri229\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24  8.    \expnd7\expndtw34  \expnd0\expndtw0 When making decisions it is difficult to fully represent possibilities using only\f30  sounds, words or feelings.  \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 he visual system is helpful, because it enables one to\f30  simultaneously picture different options and make comparisons between them.\par\pard\sl-166\slmult0\fs16 \par\pard\li104\sl-240\slmult0\f30\fs24  9.    \expnd7\expndtw34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Kinesthetic tactile and proprioceptive sensations help provide raw data.\par\pard\sl-166\slmult0\fs16 \par\pard\li104\sl-240\slmult0\f30\fs24 10.    \expnd-8\expndtw-39  \expnd0\expndtw0 Kinesthetic Meta is the primary way people evaluate experience.\par\pard\sl-126\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\li104\ri423\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24 11.    \expnd-8\expndtw-39  \expnd0\expndtw0 Congruent feelings are perceptual feelings of events, involving direct tactile\f30  and proprioceptive sensations.  \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 hey are purely perceptual or sensory experiences\f30  without evaluations.\par\pard\sl-126\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\li104\ri158\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24 12.    \expnd-8\expndtw-39  \expnd0\expndtw0 Meta-feelings are evaluative feelings about events in response to criteria, and\f30  usually have a positive or negative value.  \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 hey are what we usually call emotions or\f30  feeling states.  Meta-feelings may be created through past anchoring of experiences\f30  and/or beliefs.\par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-118\slmult0\fs10 \par\pard\li5154\sl-200\slmult0\f30\fs20\expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 h\expnd0\expndtw0 e\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 NLP\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Mas\expnd0\expndtw-2 t\expnd0\expndtw0 e\expnd0\expndtw-2 r \expnd0\expndtw0 P\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 ac\expnd0\expndtw-2 titi\expnd0\expndtw0 o\expnd-1\expndtw-3 n\expnd0\expndtw0 e\expnd0\expndtw-2 r \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 aining\expnd0\expndtw-2 ,  \expnd0\expndtw0 July\expnd0\expndtw-2 , \expnd0\expndtw0 2004\par\pard\li3695\sl-240\slmult0\sb8\f30\fs20\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Copy\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 ight \f47\charscalex107 ©\f30\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100  \expnd0\expndtw0 1987-2004\expnd0\expndtw-2 , \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 ad\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 James\expnd0\expndtw-2 , \expnd0\expndtw0 Advanced\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Neu\expnd0\expndtw-2 r\expnd0\expndtw0 o\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Dynamics\par\pard\sect\sectd\sbkpage\marglsxn1480\margrsxn600\margtsxn760\cols2\colno1\colw6977\colsr1602\colno2\colw1581\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-233\slmult0\fs22 \par\pard\li3269\sl-280\slmult0\f75\fs28\i1\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex99 MO\expnd1\expndtw3 T\expnd-2\expndtw-11 I\expnd0\expndtw-2 VA\expnd1\expndtw3 T\expnd-2\expndtw-11 I\expnd0\expndtw-2 O\expnd0\expndtw0 N \expnd0\expndtw-2 S\expnd1\expndtw3 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 RA\expnd1\expndtw3 T\expnd0\expndtw-2 EG\expnd-2\expndtw-11 I\expnd0\expndtw-2 E\expnd0\expndtw0 S\i0\charscalex100 \par\pard\sl-360\slmult0\sb14 \column \f26\fs36 Six\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 …\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 15\par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-138\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\sect\sectd\sbknone\marglsxn1480\margrsxn600\sl-264\slmult0\fs26 \par\pard\li104\sl-240\slmult0\f30\fs24 People either move toward or away.  People who move toward too strongly may\par\pard\li104\ri152\sl-280\slmult0\sb7\f30\fs24 never get around to doing unpleasant things which are necessary.  People who move\f30  away may never move until things get worse rather than better.  \expnd-1\expndtw-3 T\expnd0\expndtw0 he key to\f30  motivation is to be able easily and effortlessly to do things that are unpleasant.\par\pard\li104\sl-240\slmult0\sb47\f30\fs24 Most people do not need help in doing things that are pleasant.\par\pard\sl-173\slmult0\fs16 \par\pard
