\li3608\ri3623\qc\sl-360\slmult0\f90\fs36\b1\expnd0\expndtw-2 Spelling\expnd0\expndtw0  \expnd0\expndtw-2 Elicitation\b0\expnd0\expndtw0 \par\pard\sl-294\slmult0\fs28 \par\pard\li643\fi-520\ri170\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24 1.   \expnd-7\expndtw-34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Start at the beginning.  “When I give you the word .... what is the first thing you\f30  do on the inside?”\par\pard\li643\fi-520\ri1149\sl-280\slmult0\sb7\f30\fs24 2.   \expnd-7\expndtw-34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Backtrack and go on.  “So first you ... and then what?”  Make sure they\f30  behaviorally follow you with each step.\par\pard\li124\sl-240\slmult0\sb47\f30\fs24 3.   \expnd-7\expndtw-34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Make sure that you get a step(s) that has to do with how to spell the word.\par\pard\li643\sl-240\slmult0\sb47\f30\fs24 (Some bad spellers do not have one.)  “So how do you know how to spell ...?”\par\pard\li124\sl-240\slmult0\sb47\f30\fs24 4.   \expnd-7\expndtw-34  \expnd0\expndtw0 “When you see, hear or feel that how do you know that it is right?”\par\pard\li124\sl-240\slmult0\sb47\f30\fs24 5.   \expnd-7\expndtw-34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Get only as much detail as you need.\par\pard\sl-293\slmult0\fs28 \par\pard\li104\ri287\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24 Bad spellers are made not born.  Bad spellers are not learning disabled.  They were\f30  teaching-disabled.\par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-140\slmult0\fs14 \par\pard
