\li3586\ri3603\qc\sl-360\slmult0\f90\fs36\b1 Common Problems\b0 \par\pard\sl-294\slmult0\fs28 \par\pard\li643\fi-520\ri358\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24 1.   \expnd-7\expndtw-34  \expnd0\expndtw0 People try to create the word while looking in visual remember.  “Look up here\f30  and wait until you see the word the way you have seen it before.  Allow the\f30  image to pop up.”\par\pard\sl-293\slmult0\fs28 \par\pard\li643\fi-520\ri150\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24 2.   \expnd-7\expndtw-34  \expnd0\expndtw0 If people draw a blank, write out the word and hold it up in visual remember.\f30  Have them look at it and then close their eyes and see it internally as a memory\f30  image.\par\pard\sl-293\slmult0\fs28 \par\pard\li643\fi-520\ri233\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24 3.   \expnd-7\expndtw-34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Hold the word up for a short period.  If too long some people will try to describe\f30  it rather than see it.\par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-133\slmult0\fs12 \par\pard\li124\sl-240\slmult0\f30\fs24 4.   \expnd-7\expndtw-34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Have them visualize the word on something that they can remember easily.\par\pard\sl-293\slmult0\fs28 \par\pard\li643\fi-520\ri572\qj\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24 5.     \expnd3\expndtw14  \expnd0\expndtw0 A person keeps going back to their old strategy rather than using the new\f30  one.  Reframe the persistent voice.  If first step is a negative K, then create a\f30  resource anchor (or use a dissociated-state rehearsal if necessary).\par\pard\sl-293\slmult0\fs28 \par\pard\li643\fi-520\ri314\sl-280\slmult0\f30\fs24 6.   \expnd-7\expndtw-34  \expnd0\expndtw0 Client may have created a part responsible for spelling, and not have access to\f30  it.\par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20 \par\pard\sl-200\slmult0\fs20